            "title": "Read models/simple_baseline.py",
            "status": "completed",
            "kind": "read",
            "raw_output": "1\t\"\"\"\n2\tA simple linear regression model to be used as a baseline for flare forecasting.\n3\t\"\"\"\n4\t\n5\timport torch\n6\timport torch.nn as nn\n7\tfrom einops import rearrange\n8\t\n9\t\n10\tdef destandardize_channels(batch: dict, channel_order: list, scalers: dict) -> dict:\n11\t    \"\"\"Return a new batch dict with 'ts' moved from normalized space to signum-log space.\n12\t\n13\t    This undoes the per-channel z-score ONLY. The signum-log compression applied by the\n14\t    dataset is deliberately left in place, so the result is\n15\t    ``sign(x*s) * log1p(|x*s|)`` \u2014 not raw DN/Gauss. Values spanning many orders of\n16\t    magnitude make poor features for a single linear layer, so log space is what the\n17\t    baseline wants.\n18\t\n19\t    If you need true physical units (plotting, a physical-space loss), use\n20\t    ``HelioNetCDFDataset.inverse_transform_data()`` instead, which undoes both stages.\n21\t    See the \"THE THREE SPACES\" block in ``workshop_infrastructure/datasets/helio.py``.\n22\t\n23\t    Args:\n24\t        batch: Batch dict containing at minimum a 'ts' key with shape (B, C, T, H, W).\n25\t        channel_order: Channel names in the same order as the C dimension of 'ts'.\n26\t        scalers: Dict mapping channel name -> scaler with an inverse_transform method.\n27\t\n28\t    Returns:\n29\t        A new batch dict with 'ts' replaced by the de-standardized (signum-log) tensor.\n30\t    \"\"\"\n31\t    x = batch[\"ts\"].clone()\n32\t    with torch.no_grad():\n33\t        for i, channel in enumerate(channel_order):\n34\t            x[:, i, ...] = scalers[channel].inverse_transform(x[:, i, ...])\n35\t    return {**batch, \"ts\": x}\n36\t\n37\t\n38\tclass IdentificationModel(nn.Module):\n39\t    def __init__(self, input_dim: int):\n40\t        \"\"\"\n41\t        Initializes the Solar Event Identification model which helps predict the occurrence of a solar event.\n42\t\n43\t        Args:\n44\t            input_dim (int): The size of the input vector after channel and time dimensions are flattened.\n45\t\n46\t        Note:\n47\t            This model expects 'ts' in the batch dict to already be in **signum-log** space\n48\t            (channel z-scores undone, log compression retained). Use\n49\t            destandardize_channels() to pre-process normalized SDO inputs before passing\n50\t            them here (e.g., via the preprocess_fn argument of FlareLightningModule).\n51\t        \"\"\"\n52\t        super().__init__()\n53\t        self.linear = nn.Linear(input_dim, 1)\n54\t\n55\t    def forward(self, x: dict) -> torch.Tensor:\n56\t        \"\"\"\n57\t        Performs a forward pass through the model.\n58\t\n59\t        Args:\n60\t            x (dict): Batch dict with 'ts' of shape (B, C, T, H, W) in signum-log space.\n61\t\n62\t        B - Batch size\n63\t        C - Channels\n64\t        T - Time steps\n65\t        H - Height\n66\t        W - Width\n67\t        \"\"\"\n68\t        x = x[\"ts\"]\n69\t\n70\t        # Collapse input stack spatially and take absolute value for strictly positive flare fluxes\n71\t        x = x.abs().mean(dim=[3, 4])\n72\t\n73\t        # Rearrange in preparation for linear layer\n74\t        x = rearrange(x, \"b c t -> b (c t)\")\n75\t\n76\t        return self.linear(x)",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_012mmYPABpTbg88CfbDKdeK3",
            "locations": [
              "/home/jovyan/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/solar_event/models/simple_baseline.py"
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw_output": "137:# THE THREE SPACES  (read this before writing any \"inverse transform\" code)\n138-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n139-#\n140-# The forward pipeline has two stages, so there are three meaningful spaces \u2014 and\n141-# therefore two different things \"undoing the transform\" can mean. Conflating them is\n142-# the easiest way to feed a model silently wrong numbers.\n143-#\n144-#   normalized     What the dataset returns and the model sees. Roughly zero-mean,\n145-#                  unit-variance per channel.\n146-#      |\n147-#      |  StandardScaler.inverse_transform()      <- undoes the z-score ONLY\n148-#      v\n149-#   signum-log     sign(x\u00b7s)\u00b7log1p(|x\u00b7s|). Still log-compressed, but channels are back\n150-#                  on their own scales. This is the linear baseline's feature space\n151-#                  (see downstream_apps/template/models/simple_baseline.py:\n152-#                  destandardize_channels).\n153-#      |\n154-#      |  StandardScaler.inverse_signum_log_transform()\n155-#      v\n156-#   physical       Raw instrument units \u2014 DN for AIA, Gauss for HMI, m/s for Doppler.\n157-#                  What you want for plotting with real colour limits, or for a loss\n158-#                  expressed in physical units.\n159-#\n160-# ``HelioNetCDFDataset.inverse_transform_data()`` goes from normalized all the way to\n161-# physical in one step (both stages), which is why notebook 0 can plot its output with\n162-# real DN percentiles and \u00b11000 G magnetogram limits.\n163-#\n164-# So: ``scaler.inverse_transform()`` is NOT the inverse of the dataset's ``transform()``.\n165-# It is the inverse of only the second stage. Name variables for the space they hold.\n166-#\n167-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------",
            "permission_status": "resolved",
            "title": "grep -n \"THREE SPACES\" -A 30 helio.py | head -50",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01AD7Upvt14SYFTxKbTnDN9p",
            "selected_option_id": "allow-once",
            "session_id": "9bc63130-94c9-4af9-b64c-dcb748155e8c",
            "status": "completed",
            "raw_input": {
              "command": "grep -n \"THREE SPACES\" -A 30 /home/jovyan/surya_workshop/workshop_infrastructure/datasets/helio.py | head -50"
            },
            "kind": "execute",
            "permission_options": [
